#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100642 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dbb4e0a0-55ec-5cc7-9617-99cec8108940" :question/math-academy-id "e-540" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100646 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "891e9004-961b-539a-ab93-0752347fd077" :question/math-academy-id "e-541" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dc3f3e0-ff57-5efd-bd2a-2ae7c331785c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290335} {:answer/id #uuid "13cc58bb-55ce-5b90-bc27-e0d82b697e61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290336} {:answer/id #uuid "c22f6665-5738-56da-b581-b8d90a921abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290337} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf097b4-cf1f-5a26-939d-f3154132a89b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y=-2x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290338} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1214e9-480e-5e00-9d58-fabbe34483df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13cc58bb-55ce-5b90-bc27-e0d82b697e61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290336} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb92c282-cf61-5b85-93a2-fb47c1fb258d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a2470563-1a2f-5e0a-b7d9-e6883d815fd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104055" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =x+C \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =-x-C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-0-C \\\\ 0 & =0-C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290340 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bc12d2e-e51b-5a42-96cd-b305f65fb37f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290342} {:answer/id #uuid "db1c7f3a-6ecc-55c5-809a-0863430e9877" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290343} {:answer/id #uuid "98c45658-526f-5c3d-a7a4-904eaec5c7b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290344} {:answer/id #uuid "eb56b96c-6b1e-5509-9c5c-9596df9d1218" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290345} {:answer/id #uuid "9123b0fe-37e0-53a2-b9b6-a4027f596f01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bc12d2e-e51b-5a42-96cd-b305f65fb37f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290342} :answer-field/id #uuid "062b6761-8a83-56a7-ab24-c797cc9067ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76f508a1-f65b-5d1d-8bbf-94be0b492cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-104064" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{4}-{2}^{3}-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4f4d250-d63c-5e5d-9611-c2c1acc8c318" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290349} {:answer/id #uuid "2e605334-fa8a-5fc8-84ae-745241f7e87b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x+{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290350} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4121d6-bab1-56e1-abd4-3bf6e7a40176" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2x-{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290351} {:answer/id #uuid "8737c814-c6ba-5785-8955-54b94b08fc8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290352} {:answer/id #uuid "b247558b-3f44-596b-8b69-4a7a26fdabe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8737c814-c6ba-5785-8955-54b94b08fc8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290352} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a2c8b3-5c91-581b-a5a1-77684e23bbb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89b29480-9c98-5ccc-8d03-beba2594d431" :question/math-academy-id "q-14267" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x+y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}{e}^{y} \\\\ {e}^{-y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{-y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{-y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -{e}^{-y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{-y} & =-{e}^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ -y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{x}) \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{0}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ C-1 & =2 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16561ff9-49cc-5c8d-9d91-80496b61032b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x^2+2)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16561ff9-49cc-5c8d-9d91-80496b61032b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x^2+2)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290356} :answer-field/id #uuid "abcfd3ba-e3c9-5721-a8d2-3b248e6bea2a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e61295b6-6138-5875-8867-aee2da069121" :question/math-academy-id "q-355528" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\sqrt{y}$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(1)=9.$  Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & =2{x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2} \\\\ y & ={({x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+C)^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=9$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =((1)^{2}+C)^{2} \\\\ 9 & =(1+C)^{2} \\\\ 3 & =1+C \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+2)^{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290357 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "048cd733-c2e8-5560-9a90-750596f21cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^2+6\\sqrt{x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "048cd733-c2e8-5560-9a90-750596f21cad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^2+6\\sqrt{x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290359} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee9a0b78-99ca-5f4b-a1cb-eda7b77e2f30" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ec860881-ff21-5e4e-8a65-6e52d2f89b50" :question/math-academy-id "q-355547" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(1)=11.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+4x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(3{x}^{-1/2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{-1/2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6{x}^{1/2}+2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=11$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =11 \\\\ 6(1)^{1/2}+2(1)^{2}+C & =11 \\\\ C+8 & =11 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =6{x}^{1/2}+2{x}^{2}+3 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{x}+2{x}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a0b9fd2-1a98-57a7-aaf0-4cd30a179d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2e^{2x^2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290362} {:answer/id #uuid "8738d267-dd21-5b3e-990b-73cdd6fd0592" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2e^{2x^2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a0b9fd2-1a98-57a7-aaf0-4cd30a179d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2e^{2x^2}-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290362} :answer-field/id #uuid "82fc8af0-57e3-5be9-8c92-d5f15f62151b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c2662fd-a3c2-5d7c-b983-4e24453e056f" :question/math-academy-id "q-355559" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x{y}^{2}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$ Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x{y}^{2} & =4x \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x{y}^{2}+4x \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x({y}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1) & =2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExponentiating both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)} & ={e}^{2{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ {y}^{2}+1 & =C{e}^{2{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt{C{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{C{e}^{2(0)^{2}}-1} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{C-1} & =1 \\\\ C-1 & =1 \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\sqrt{2{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de2e3a7c-d4f0-5b0f-8014-1519fb3a9473" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by First Rearranging and Then Separating"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78623355-e38a-5ca6-82fc-0ede5c4c9a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78623355-e38a-5ca6-82fc-0ede5c4c9a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290366} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c75e092-6079-5be0-bdeb-81cf428bb1cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed0df24d-07b8-5d65-9f2d-72f21abe2584" :question/math-academy-id "q-355577" :question/problem "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fa13493-411e-5b0f-83c5-a1c4a3c4c5d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3} = x^{2} + \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099451} {:answer/id #uuid "a1cfa395-8414-50b1-8224-cb9e8d291a57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3} = \\frac{1}{3}x^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099452} {:answer/id #uuid "d8996977-d1af-5583-8f78-5ac2870cf12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3} = 3x^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099453} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7d3a5a-6085-5ac7-984b-91d90200a4c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3} = x^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099454} {:answer/id #uuid "2b0b73fb-ed0c-52e6-b550-92b6c60a3048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3} = \\frac{1}{6}x^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8996977-d1af-5583-8f78-5ac2870cf12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y^{3} = 3x^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099453} :answer-field/id #uuid "238b4ed3-3283-5aaf-a6ab-0b987124f5dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c894685-37ff-5d18-b9c8-6edb0d037176" :question/math-academy-id "q-4019" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}.$" :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =3{x}^{2}+3{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}$  is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{13})}^{3} & =3(2)^{2}+C \\\\ 13 & =12+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$ is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4641fa43-5ee8-5a98-a998-8306f96eab45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290369} {:answer/id #uuid "d67abf21-4258-5d25-a6bf-4116fb2dc38a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290370} {:answer/id #uuid "ebc01640-f9b4-5f31-9081-7b2cadc0f221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290371} {:answer/id #uuid "d3937128-3f8b-53e0-91dc-8c5fd9f9b870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2x-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290372} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb4d639-0119-517a-9dff-02201f38f90f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{2}{x}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d67abf21-4258-5d25-a6bf-4116fb2dc38a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290370} :answer-field/id #uuid "a51a5481-c1f2-538c-bf44-ea05615e2d8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eab8a97a-f952-5f16-9442-1a3ecf58a82a" :question/math-academy-id "q-50220" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{1+C} \\\\ 1+C & =1 \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "99112850-043d-53e5-8d61-fecb0317bd11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Particular Solutions of Differential Equations by Separating the Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f9f1a5-f46a-52b5-808c-b763c4421c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290376} {:answer/id #uuid "01cde3e0-f862-5b29-80fd-e43104620586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290377} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f769f3-c488-5e60-8b10-e07de00a892f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290378} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc5f637-d6a4-59de-b6d2-103abdf33cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290379} {:answer/id #uuid "952d6638-c733-51a4-82c1-b8f542a4dbcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5f769f3-c488-5e60-8b10-e07de00a892f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290378} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddd55144-c2ba-57a4-82ec-bee36392a6bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "65fc80a1-7721-5e98-9055-6f369b27046a" :question/math-academy-id "q-8309" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)} \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\ \\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}=2C.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find ${C}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the above equation as\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)).\n$$"}]}
